msgid "Detected setup"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:930
msgid "A suggestion based on your own current request, with “Matches your setting” or “Recommended: change the setting below”, and the IP address Authlify sees for you right now. It never changes the setting by itself."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:931
msgid "Directly (default)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:931
msgid "Uses the connecting address. Right for sites with no proxy or CDN in front."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:932
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:110
msgid "Through Cloudflare"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:932
msgid "Uses the <code>CF-Connecting-IP</code> header, but only when the request really comes from one of Cloudflare’s published address ranges."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:933
msgid "Through my own proxy or load balancer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:933
msgid "Uses <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>, but only when the request comes from an address in <strong>Trusted proxies</strong> (one IP or CIDR range per line). It reads the header from the right and takes the first address that is not one of your proxies."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:934
msgid "After saving, “Your IP address as seen now” should show your real public address, not your host’s or Cloudflare’s. WordPress Site Health also warns when the setting and your setup disagree."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:936
msgid "The Cloudflare address ranges are built into the plugin. Cloudflare rarely changes them, but a request from a brand-new range would be treated as direct."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:937
msgid "The <code>X-Real-IP</code> header is not used."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:943
msgid "Addresses that are never locked out, and addresses that can never log in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:945
#, php-format
msgid "%s, panel <strong>Allow and block lists</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:947
msgid "<strong>Never lock out</strong>: your office or home IP. Failures from these addresses are not counted, they are never locked out, and they never see a CAPTCHA."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:948
msgid "<strong>Always block</strong>: these addresses can never log in. They get “Access from your network is blocked.” They can still view the site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:949
msgid "One IPv4 or IPv6 address or CIDR range per line (commas also work), for example <code>203.0.113.7</code>, <code>198.51.100.0/24</code> or <code>2001:db8::/32</code>. Invalid entries are refused when you save."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:950
msgid "You cannot save a block list that contains your own current address."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:952
msgid "Both lists only apply while brute-force protection is on. They use the address from the Visitor IP setting, so set that first."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:957
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:47
msgid "Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:957
msgid "Close the other ways into WordPress: XML-RPC, application passwords, username discovery and revealing error messages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:958
#, php-format
msgid "Where: %s. Every option here is off (the WordPress default) until you change it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:960
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1468
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:170
#: inc/Diagnostics/LeakCheck.php:376
#: inc/Diagnostics/SiteHealth.php:448
msgid "XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:961
msgid "<strong>On</strong> (default): unchanged. Some apps and Jetpack need it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:962
msgid "<strong>On, but block multi-password requests</strong>: removes <code>system.multicall</code>, which lets one request try hundreds of passwords. Such requests get an error (HTTP 403). Everything else keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:963
msgid "<strong>Off</strong>: every request to xmlrpc.php gets HTTP 403, and the pingback header and discovery link are removed. Choose it if you do not use the WordPress mobile app, Jetpack or remote publishing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:965
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1469
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:175
#: inc/Diagnostics/LeakCheck.php:379
#: inc/Diagnostics/LeakCheck.php:796
#: inc/Diagnostics/SiteHealth.php:449
msgid "Application passwords"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:965
msgid "They let apps log in through the REST API without the login page, CAPTCHA or two-factor. Choose <strong>All users</strong> (default), <strong>Administrators only</strong> (on multisite: super admins only) or <strong>Off</strong>. Brute-force limits apply to them either way."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:966
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1470
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:183
msgid "Username discovery"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:966
msgid "When on, visitors who are not logged in can no longer list usernames: the REST API users endpoints disappear, <code>?author=</code> links and author archives return “page not found”, the users sitemap is removed and oEmbed data no longer names the author. Logged-in people still see author archives."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:967
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1471
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:184
msgid "Login error messages"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:967
msgid "When on, a failed login always says “The username or password is incorrect.” instead of telling an attacker which one was wrong."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:968
#: inc/Admin/ProtectionPage.php:187
msgid "Private site"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:968
#, php-format
msgid "See %s."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:968
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:973
msgid "Force login (private site)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:973
msgid "Only logged-in users can see the site; everyone else is sent to the login page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:975
#, php-format
msgid "%s, panel <strong>Private site</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:977
msgid "<strong>Force login</strong>: “Require login to view the site” (off by default)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:978
msgid "<strong>Public pages</strong>: paths that stay public, one per line (commas also work). A path includes its sub-pages: <code>/shop</code> covers <code>/shop/</code> and <code>/shop/item</code>, but not <code>/shopping</code>. Use <code>/</code> for the home page only. Full URLs are accepted; only the path is used. There are no wildcards."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:981
msgid "Visitors who are not logged in are redirected to your login address, and come back to the page they wanted after logging in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:982
msgid "Anonymous REST API requests get a “You must be logged in to use this site.” error (HTTP 401)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:983
msgid "The login page itself, robots.txt, admin-ajax and scheduled tasks keep working. RSS feeds are redirected too."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:986
msgid "Because every visitor is sent to the login page, the custom login address is no longer secret on a private site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:987
msgid "XML-RPC is not affected. Set it to Off on the same tab if you do not need it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:988
msgid "Pages that other services must reach (payment callbacks, webhooks, a WooCommerce shop) need a Public pages entry."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1004
msgid "Authlify → Security → CAPTCHA"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1007
msgid "CAPTCHA, modes and safety"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1007
msgid "Stop scripts at the form, choose when people see the check, and decide what happens if the provider is down."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1009
msgid "A CAPTCHA stops scripts that guess passwords, create fake accounts or post spam before they reach WordPress. Lockouts react after failures; a CAPTCHA stops many attempts from counting at all."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1010
#, php-format
msgid "%s, with three panels: CAPTCHA provider, Where and when, and Safety."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1011
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1484
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:191
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:192
msgid "Forms"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1011
msgid "Login, Registration and Lost password are ticked by default once a provider is chosen. You can also protect comments from visitors who are not logged in, and, when WooCommerce is active, its login, registration, lost password and classic checkout (guest orders) forms."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1011
msgid "Logins through XML-RPC, the REST API and application passwords cannot show a CAPTCHA; the brute-force limits cover those."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1012
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1485
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:217
msgid "When to show it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1012
msgid "Always (default)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1012
msgid "Every protected form shows the check."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1013
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:219
msgid "Only after failed logins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1013
msgid "The WordPress and WooCommerce login forms show it only after “Failed logins before it appears” (default 2) failures from the visitor’s address, or when the username is under attack from many addresses (the targeted-account threshold on the Brute force tab). Other forms always show it. Honest visitors who type their password correctly never see it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1014
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:232
msgid "Safety"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1015
msgid "<strong>Test mode</strong> (off by default): the widget is shown and every answer is checked, but failures are only logged; nobody is blocked. This also applies to the honeypot. The panel then counts how many submissions would have been blocked in the last 7 days (this needs the activity log to be on)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1016
msgid "<strong>If the provider is down</strong>: “Let people through” (default; the brute-force limits still apply) or “Block the form until the provider is back”. A provider counts as down when it cannot be reached within 8 seconds or returns a server error. Outages are recorded in the activity log."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1017
msgid "<strong>Honeypot</strong>: see the honeypot article."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1020
msgid "The provider’s script loads only on pages that show a protected form."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1021
msgid "A failed check shows an error on the form and is logged as “CAPTCHA failed” with the reason. Failed CAPTCHA checks do not count towards lockouts."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1022
msgid "Addresses on “Never lock out” never see a CAPTCHA or the honeypot. Logged-in people never see one on comments or checkout."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1023
msgid "The dashboard counts CAPTCHA as done when a provider is set up for the login form and test mode is off."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1025
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1149
msgid "Emergency switch"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1025
msgid "If a CAPTCHA ever stops you logging in, add this to wp-config.php, log in and fix the settings, then remove it:"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1026
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1030
msgid "CAPTCHA providers"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1026
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1603
msgid "Add a CAPTCHA without blocking real people"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1030
msgid "Cloudflare Turnstile, ALTCHA, hCaptcha and Google reCAPTCHA v2 and v3: what each needs and what it sends where."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1032
msgid "Choosing"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1032
msgid "Turnstile suits most sites. Choose ALTCHA if nothing may be sent to another company. You can switch at any time."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1033
msgid "Cloudflare Turnstile (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1033
msgid "Free and usually shows no puzzle at all. It does not need Cloudflare hosting. Create a widget under Cloudflare dashboard → Turnstile and paste its site key and secret key. The visitor’s browser loads the widget from challenges.cloudflare.com, and your server confirms each answer there."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1034
msgid "ALTCHA (no third party)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1034
msgid "Runs entirely on your site: no keys, no cookies and nothing sent elsewhere. The browser solves a small proof-of-work puzzle in the background, and your server checks it; each answer works once. It needs JavaScript, and it cannot have an outage."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1035
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:136
#: inc/Captcha/HCaptcha.php:32
msgid "hCaptcha"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1035
msgid "Privacy-focused with a free plan; it shows image puzzles more often than Turnstile. Keys come from the hCaptcha dashboard → Sites. The widget loads from js.hcaptcha.com and answers are checked at api.hcaptcha.com."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1036
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:137
#: inc/Captcha/RecaptchaV2.php:32
msgid "Google reCAPTCHA v2"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1036
msgid "The “I’m not a robot” checkbox. Keys come from the Google reCAPTCHA admin console; pick the v2 checkbox type. It sends visitor data to Google, and free-tier limits apply."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1037
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:138
#: inc/Captcha/RecaptchaV3.php:35
msgid "Google reCAPTCHA v3"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1037
msgid "Invisible: Google scores each visit from 0.0 (bot) to 1.0 (human), and visits below the <strong>Minimum score</strong> (default 0.5) are refused. It can quietly block real people, with no puzzle to prove otherwise. v2 keys do not work with v3."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1038
msgid "Saving keys safely"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1039
msgid "Paste both keys, click <strong>Show preview</strong> and complete the check. The provider’s script loads only when you click."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1040
msgid "When you save, Authlify checks the secret key with the provider using that preview answer. A wrong key is refused and nothing is saved, so a typo cannot lock anyone out."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1041
msgid "Saving without completing the preview is refused, unless test mode is on (then it saves with a warning). If the provider cannot be reached, the keys are saved with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1042
msgid "Answers solved on another website are refused: the provider must confirm your site’s own domain."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1048
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1489
#: inc/Captcha/Admin.php:246
msgid "Honeypot"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1048
msgid "An invisible trap that catches simple bots without asking people anything."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1050
#, php-format
msgid "%s, panel <strong>Safety</strong>, <strong>Honeypot</strong> (off by default)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1052
msgid "It adds a hidden field to the same forms the CAPTCHA protects. People, screen readers and password managers never see it; bots that fill in every field do."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1053
msgid "It also adds a signed time stamp. A form sent back in under 2 seconds, with a missing or altered stamp, with a stamp older than a day, or with a stamp already used, is refused."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1054
msgid "It works with or without a CAPTCHA provider."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1056
msgid "A honeypot stops simple scripts, not determined attackers. Use it together with lockouts, and a CAPTCHA where spam is a problem."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1071
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1560
msgid "Authlify → Two-factor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1074
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1499
#: inc/Security/Passwords.php:426
msgid "Breached-password check"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1074
msgid "Refuse new passwords that appear in known data breaches, without ever sending the password anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1076
#, php-format
msgid "%s, panel <strong>Breached passwords</strong>. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1076
msgid "Authlify → Security → Passwords"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1078
msgid "<strong>Breached-password check</strong>: “Refuse passwords found in known data breaches”."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1079
msgid "<strong>Roles</strong>: tick the roles to check. Leave all unticked to check everyone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1081
msgid "Whenever a password is set: on profile screens (your own, editing a user, adding a user), password resets, registration forms that ask for a password, and WooCommerce registration, account details and checkout account creation. It does not run at login, so existing passwords keep working."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1082
msgid "How the password stays private"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1082
msgid "Authlify hashes the password with SHA-1 and sends only the first 5 characters of that hash to the Have I Been Pwned “range” service (api.pwnedpasswords.com). The service answers with every breached hash starting with those characters, padded with decoys, and Authlify compares the rest on your server. Neither the password nor its full hash leaves your site. Answers are cached for a day."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1083
msgid "A breached password is refused with “This password has appeared N times in known data breaches, so attackers try it early. Please choose a different password.” and logged as “Breached password refused”. If the service cannot be reached within 3 seconds, the password is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1088
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1496
#: inc/Admin/ProPage.php:109
#: inc/Admin/UI.php:450
#: inc/Admin/UI.php:451
#: inc/Diagnostics/SiteHealth.php:452
#: inc/TwoFactor/AdminPage.php:81
#: inc/TwoFactor/AdminPage.php:114
#: inc/TwoFactor/LoginFlow.php:156
#: inc/TwoFactor/LoginFlow.php:702
#: inc/TwoFactor/Profile.php:227
msgid "Two-factor login"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1088
msgid "A second step after the password: an authenticator app, a passkey or a backup code."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1090
msgid "A stolen or guessed password is not enough to get in when the account also needs a code from the owner’s phone or a passkey on their device."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1091
#, php-format
msgid "Settings: %s. Each person sets it up under <strong>Users → Profile → Two-factor login</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1093
msgid "<strong>Two-factor login</strong> (on by default): lets people turn it on. When off, nobody is asked for a second step and the profile section is hidden; existing setups are kept."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1094
msgid "<strong>Offered methods</strong>: Authenticator app, Backup codes, Passkeys and security keys. Turning a method off stops new setups; people who already use it keep it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1095
msgid "<strong>Passkey sign-in</strong>: see the passkeys article."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1097
msgid "Setting it up (each person)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1098
msgid "<strong>Authenticator app</strong>: click “Set up an authenticator app”, scan the QR code with Google Authenticator, 1Password, Authy or a similar app, enter the 6-digit code and click “Verify and turn on”."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1099
msgid "<strong>Backup codes</strong>: 10 one-time codes are created automatically after the first method. Save them: they are shown once. Each works once; you are warned when two or fewer are left, and “Create new codes” replaces the whole set."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1100
msgid "<strong>Passkeys</strong>: click “Add a passkey” and follow the browser’s prompt."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1102
msgid "Signing in"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1103
msgid "After the correct password, the “Confirm it’s you” step asks for the code (or the passkey). “Having trouble?” switches to another method, such as a backup code."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1104
msgid "Codes from an authenticator app work once; a code that was just used is refused. After 5 wrong codes the person has to sign in again, and wrong codes count towards brute-force lockouts."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1105
msgid "“Remember me” from the password step is kept. The free plugin has no “trust this device” option."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1106
msgid "Logins from the WooCommerce My Account form and other front-end forms continue to the same step."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1107
msgid "Apps that log in with the account password over XML-RPC or the REST API are refused for people with two-factor; they must use an application password."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1109
msgid "Who uses it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1109
msgid "The Two-factor screen lists, per role, how many people use two-factor (backup codes alone do not count), and the Users list gets a “2FA” column. The dashboard checklist shows how many administrators use it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1111
msgid "In the free plugin two-factor is opt-in; it cannot be required for a role."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1112
msgid "If another two-factor plugin is active (Two Factor, WP 2FA or Wordfence Login Security), Authlify steps aside and says so."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1113
msgid "Authenticator secrets are encrypted with keys derived from your wp-config.php security keys. Changing <code>AUTH_KEY</code> or <code>SECURE_AUTH_SALT</code> makes them unreadable, so people then need a backup code, a passkey or a reset."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1115
#: inc/TwoFactor/Profile.php:152
#: inc/TwoFactor/TwoFactor.php:257
#: inc/TwoFactor/TwoFactor.php:297
msgid "Passkeys"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1115
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1557
msgid "Require two-factor for administrators"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1119
#: inc/TwoFactor/AdminPage.php:122
msgid "Passkeys and security keys"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1119
msgid "Sign in with a fingerprint, face, screen lock or hardware key, as a second step or instead of the password."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1122
msgid "PHP 8.0 or newer on the server. On older PHP the option is greyed out on the Two-factor screen, with the version shown."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1123
msgid "https (or localhost while developing), and a browser or device that supports passkeys."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1125
msgid "Setting one up"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1125
msgid "Under <strong>Users → Profile → Two-factor login</strong>, click <strong>Add a passkey</strong>, confirm with the device, and give it a name such as “MacBook Touch ID”. Passkeys can be renamed or removed there."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1126
msgid "Using it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1127
msgid "<strong>As the second step</strong>: after the password, choose “Use my passkey”."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1128
msgid "<strong>Instead of the password</strong>: with <strong>Passkey sign-in</strong> on (the default), the login form shows “Sign in with a passkey” once anyone on the site has added one, in browsers that support passkeys. It counts as both factors and needs the device’s PIN or biometric."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1129
msgid "Passkey sign-in respects lockouts; failures are logged but do not count as wrong passwords."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1132
msgid "A passkey belongs to the site’s domain. After moving the site to another domain, everyone must add their passkeys again."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1133
msgid "Passkeys are stored as public keys only; the private key never leaves the person’s device."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1139
msgid "What to do when someone loses their phone and backup codes."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1141
msgid "Recovery email (self-service)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1142
msgid "On the two-factor step, “Can’t use your methods? Email me a recovery link” sends a link to the account’s email address. It is also available from a separate “Account recovery” form, which asks for the username or email and the password."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1143
msgid "The link works once, for 15 minutes, and replaces any earlier link. At most 3 links per account per hour (and 5 requests per address per hour from the separate form)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1144
msgid "Opening it shows a confirmation page first, so email scanners cannot use it. It signs the person in once and takes them to their profile to set up a new method. Their existing methods are kept, and the site admin address is notified."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1145
msgid "It is only offered after a correct password and when the account has a valid email address."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1147
msgid "Reset by an administrator"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1147
#, php-format
msgid "%s → <strong>Reset for a user</strong>: find the person by username or email and click <strong>Reset</strong>. It removes their authenticator app, backup codes and passkeys (you never see their secrets), so they can sign in with their password and set up again. Administrators can also use “Reset two-factor login” on the person’s profile."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1148
#: inc/Admin/ProPage.php:141
#: inc/Diagnostics/LeakCheck.php:1211
msgid "WP-CLI"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1149
msgid "This turns two-factor off for everyone without deleting anything. Remove it as soon as you are back in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1154
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1599
msgid "Login page designer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1154
msgid "Style every login screen to match your site, with templates, “Match my site” and a live preview."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1156
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1594
msgid "Authlify → Designer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1157
