#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1166
msgid "<strong>More actions</strong>: revert to saved, reset to the Default template, start from plain WordPress, export the design as JSON, or import one."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1169
msgid "Nothing changes on a new site until you switch a design on and save."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1170
msgid "The styles are compiled into a small CSS file in <code>wp-content/uploads/authlify/</code>, or printed inline if that folder is not writable."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1171
msgid "Custom CSS is limited to 20,000 characters, and anything that could run scripts or load remote styles is removed."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1172
msgid "Sites upgraded from Modify Login 2.x keep their old look. Designs from LoginPress and Colorlib Login Customizer can be imported under Authlify → Settings; imported designs go live immediately."
