#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1195
msgid "<strong>By role</strong>: open a role to give it its own addresses. Empty fields use the addresses for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1196
msgid "Use <code>{username}</code> or <code>{user_id}</code> in an address, for example <code>/members/{username}/</code>. <code>{username}</code> is the person’s URL-friendly name (their “nicename”), not necessarily the name they log in with."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1198
msgid "Which address wins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1199
msgid "After login: a specific destination in the login link (<code>redirect_to</code>) wins, unless it is just the dashboard. Then the first of the person’s roles that has a rule, then the address for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1200
msgid "After logout: a specific destination in the logout link always wins, then the role rule, then the address for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1201
msgid "People who cannot use the dashboard are sent to the homepage instead of a wp-admin address."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1203
msgid "Only addresses on this site, or on hosts your site allows for redirects, are used. Anything else falls back to the WordPress default."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1208
msgid "Every login, failed attempt, lockout and security change, stored only in your own database."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1210
#, php-format
msgid "%s, with a <strong>Log</strong> tab and a <strong>Settings</strong> tab. The dashboard shows the last eight entries and seven-day totals."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1210
msgid "Authlify → Activity"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1211
msgid "What is recorded"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1211
msgid "Logins, failed logins, lockouts and unlocks, blocked addresses, CAPTCHA failures, logouts, password resets, login address changes, log clearing, two-factor and passkey events, recovery emails, and refused breached passwords. Each entry keeps the time, event, user, username, IP address, browser (user agent), country when known, and details such as the channel (login form, XML-RPC, REST API or WooCommerce) and the reason for a failure."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1212
msgid "Using the log"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1213
msgid "Filter by event, by date range, or search for a username or IP address. Clicking an IP address searches for it (a partial match, so 1.2.3.4 also finds 1.2.3.45)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1214
msgid "<strong>Export CSV</strong> downloads the filtered entries (up to 100,000 rows). Cells that could be read as spreadsheet formulas are neutralised."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1215
msgid "50 entries per page, with Newer and Older buttons."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1218
msgid "<strong>Activity log</strong> (on by default). Lockouts still work when it is off. Login address changes are always recorded."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1219
msgid "<strong>Keep entries for</strong> 90 days by default; older entries are deleted daily. 0 keeps them forever."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1220
msgid "<strong>Anonymize IPs</strong> (off by default): stores IPv4 addresses without their last part (203.0.113.0) and keeps only the first half of IPv6 addresses. Lockouts still use full addresses."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1221
msgid "<strong>Country</strong>: “Do not record”, or use the country your CDN provides. In the free plugin a country is only recorded when the Visitor IP setting is “Through Cloudflare” (Cloudflare’s country header). It is never looked up through a third-party service."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1222
msgid "<strong>Lockout email</strong> (off by default): emails the site admin address when a lockout was triggered with an administrator’s username. At most one email per hour."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1223
msgid "<strong>Delete all entries</strong> empties the log at once. It cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1225
msgid "On multisite the log is shared by the network, so each site’s Activity screen shows entries from all sites, and clearing it clears every site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1226
#, php-format
msgid "Privacy details are in %s."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1226
#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1896
msgid "Retention, anonymization and personal data requests"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Admin/Docs.php:1230
